# One window owns the screen

Subclass `ui::Window`, take `ui::Context&` and whatever you display by value, and
load in `on_focus()` — never in the constructor, since results cannot be posted
before the event loop starts. Register the new file in `CMakeLists.txt`.

Windows talk to the app only through `ui::Context`. Never include `app.hpp`.

# Return false for keys you do not own

Unhandled keys fall through to the application, which is where `q` (back), space
and Enter (confirm) and `?` (help) live. Returning `true` for everything breaks
navigation.

# Text input wins over universal keys

```cpp
// ✅ GOOD: a typed "q" or space reaches the query
if (filter_.on_event(event)) { selected_ = 0; return true; }
if (ui::motion(event, selected_, count)) return true;
if (ui::is_select(event)) { open_selected(); return true; }
```

Checking `ui::is_back` or `ui::is_select` first makes it impossible to filter for
`queue` or type a summary containing a space.

# keys() is the keymap

The footer hint line and the `?` overlay are generated from `keys()`. A binding
missing from it is invisible to the user, so add the entry in the same change as
the binding.

# Refresh quietly after an edit

Pass `announce = false` to a reload triggered by a mutation, so the status bar
keeps showing what the edit did instead of a "loaded N issues" message.
